{"pack": "m2ui", "voice": "boy", "speaker": {"am_puck": 0.8, "af_heart": 0.2}, "audio": "m2ui-20261117b.mp4", "model": "Kokoro-82M v1.0 (Apache 2.0) via kokoro-onnx (MIT); misaki phonemizer (Apache 2.0)", "gap": 0.45, "clips": {"Chapter 3 complete! Talk to Mo at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [0.0, 4.255], "Mayor Bea is waiting for you on the beach. Go and say hello!": [4.705, 3.657], "Say hello to Gus the clockmaker, on the beach.": [8.812, 2.612], "Explore Port Lumen and meet its people.": [11.874, 2.441], "Walk the Tidewalk to Port Lumen. It starts at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [14.765, 5.044], "You learned it all! Go see Gus in the Clock Tower. He heard something strange\u2026": [20.259, 4.447], "Someone is hiding up by the bells! Climb the ladder in the Clock Tower.": [25.156, 4.191], "Chapter 6 complete! Explore Port Lumen as much as you like.": [29.797, 3.999], "Help Rafi count his fish at the fish market. Count hundreds, tens and ones.": [34.245, 4.596], "Talk to Mayor Bea in the Town Hall: she has big news!": [39.291, 3.124], "Help Pedro count the people on his water taxi. He\u2019s on the Town Hall Plaza.": [42.865, 4.852], "Go see Gus in the Clock Tower. He found something!": [48.167, 3.039], "Chapter 4 complete! Now we know who sells the pages: the Crumb Crew!": [51.656, 4.255], "Chapter 5: why did the big clock stop?": [56.361, 2.548], "Chapter 5 complete! Someone took the Bell Gear to keep the bells quiet\u2026": [59.359, 4.489], "Chapter 6: who is hiding near the bells?": [64.298, 2.441], "The clock hand starts on 20. It jumps 3 tens to the right: 30, 40, 50.": [67.189, 5.791], "Count the hops: 1, 2, 3. Each hop is ten.": [73.43, 3.167], "It lands on 50! So 20 + 30 = 50.": [77.047, 3.743], "Now the hand goes back. It starts on 50 and jumps 2 tens to the LEFT: 40, 30.": [81.239, 5.855], "It lands on 30! Left means taking away: 50 \u2212 20 = 30.": [87.544, 5.193], "The hand can start between the marks, too. Start on 34 and jump 2 tens to the right: 44, 54.": [93.187, 7.476], "It lands on 54. Only the tens changed; the ones stay 4! So 34 + 20 = 54.": [101.113, 7.625], "Say hello to Mayor Bea in the Town Hall.": [109.189, 2.335], "Help Ms. Reyes read the new words on the Market Street signs!": [111.973, 3.508], "Lucy\u2019s robot fell apart on the Canal Walk. Help her build a new one!": [115.931, 4.383], "Help Captain Lin fill in her harbor book. She is on Museum Road.": [120.764, 4.02], "Walk the Tidewalk to Port Lumen! Start at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [125.234, 4.745], "Walk to the end of the old dock, to the right. The Tidewalk starts there!": [130.429, 4.169], "Cross the Tidewalk! Mina is at the first rope bridge. Win her challenge.": [135.049, 4.425], "Cadet Jo guards the second rope bridge. Win the challenge to reach Port Lumen!": [139.924, 5.193], "Keep walking east. Port Lumen\u2019s beach is just ahead!": [145.567, 3.252], "Ruby is by the broken taxi dock at the harbor. Help her fix it!": [149.269, 4.127], "You have 5 planks! Stand by the Harbor taxi stop. Press A to lay each one.": [153.846, 4.66], "Leo is waiting by the Clock Tower. Help put the loose gears back!": [158.956, 4.02], "You have 5 gears! Go into the Clock Tower. Press A by the big wheels.": [163.426, 4.063], "One question for each thing you learned on Market Street. Each right answer gives you a plank!": [167.939, 5.3], "You have all the planks! Go to the Harbor taxi stop. Press A to build the dock.": [173.689, 4.404], "One question for each thing you learned on the Canal Walk. Each right answer gives you a gear!": [178.543, 5.471], "You have all the gears! Go into the Clock Tower and press A by the big wheels.": [184.463, 4.169], "Port Lumen stamps:": [189.083, 1.332], "Still to visit in Port Lumen:": [190.865, 1.929], "Find the people with a !": [193.244, 1.503], "Port Lumen": [195.197, 1.055], "the Tidewalk": [196.701, 1.033], "A young otter with a red scarf steps out. {otter} jumps in front of you, fur up, with a little growl.": [198.185, 6.409], "Brioche stops. For a moment he just looks at {otter}.": [205.044, 3.188], "Hey, {otter} keeps looking into the water. Otters are great divers!": [208.682, 4.297], "Now {otter} can dive! Look for bubbles in the water near the shore.": [213.429, 4.127], "Brioche looks at {otter} one more time. He opens his mouth\u2026 then shuts it and runs off after the crew.": [218.006, 6.324], "Rafi has planks at the fish market.": [224.78, 2.121], "Learn with the people of Market Street, then come back!": [227.351, 3.103], "Gus says the storm knocked gears loose in the Clock Tower.": [230.904, 3.316], "Learn with the Canal Walk people!": [234.67, 1.908], "Look, {name}! The tide went out! Now there is a path of sand across the sea!": [237.028, 3.807], "This is the Tidewalk. It goes all the way to Port Lumen. That's the city on Marlo's sea chart.": [241.285, 5.876], "Explorers come here at low tide. Two of them guard the rope bridges: win their challenge to cross!": [247.611, 6.047], "Their challenges review what we learned on the island. Don\u2019t worry: if you miss, you get help and try again.": [254.107, 6.345], "THE TIDEWALK. Port Lumen \u2192 this way. Lighthouse Island \u2190 back across the dock. Walk only at low tide!": [260.903, 7.604], "THE TIDEWALK. Port Lumen, Old Town beach \u2192 right here. Lighthouse Island \u2190 across the sand and the bridges.": [268.957, 7.711], "A tide pool! When the tide goes out, sea water stays behind in the low places.": [277.117, 4.937], "Little animals wait in the pools until the sea comes back. Look, but leave them in their home.": [282.505, 5.684], "A tiny lighthouse on Little Light islet. At night it blinks, so boats don't hit the hidden sand.": [288.639, 5.855], "Gulls are resting on Gull islet. Shh\u2026 let them sleep!": [294.943, 3.785], "Halt, explorer! I\u2019m Mina. I watch the sea birds of the Tidewalk with my binoculars.": [299.179, 5.492], "This rope bridge is mine to guard. To cross, win my review challenge!": [305.121, 4.489], "It has a bit of all you learned on the island!": [310.06, 2.42], "Yes, let\u2019s play!. Not now..": [312.93, 1.631], "The bridge is open, {name}! Want to play again, just for fun?": [315.011, 3.145], "You remember so much! Here is a Tidewalk sticker for your notebook. The bridge is open!": [318.606, 4.959], "Hey, explorer! I\u2019m Milo. My kite flies best on the sandbars!": [324.015, 4.063], "Want a math challenge? Adding and taking away, up to 20. It\u2019s just for fun, you can say no!": [328.527, 6.004], "My kite is still up! Another math challenge?": [334.981, 2.719], "Wow, you\u2019re quick! Take a Tidewalk sticker!": [338.15, 2.185], "Hello, dear. I\u2019m Grandma Opal. I paint the tide pools while the sea is away.": [340.785, 4.959], "Do you like stories and words? Try my reading challenge. Only if you want to!": [346.194, 4.767], "Back for more words, dear? Another reading challenge?": [351.411, 3.017], "What a fine reader! Here is a Tidewalk sticker. I painted it myself.": [354.878, 4.041], "Shh\u2026 a crab! Oh, hi! I\u2019m Finn. I look for animals in the tide pools.": [359.369, 4.852], "Want a challenge about science and maps? Land and water, nature, and places! You can say no.": [364.671, 5.94], "Found anything in the pools? Want another science and maps challenge?": [371.061, 3.956], "You know your land and water! Here is a Tidewalk sticker!": [375.467, 3.06], "Ahoy! I\u2019m Cadet Jo of the coast watch. I keep the Tidewalk safe.": [378.977, 4.105], "To cross my bridge, show me what you learned on the island. Story problems too: first to 5 points!": [383.533, 6.345], "Miss on your first try and I get a point. Ready?": [390.328, 3.06], "The way to Port Lumen is open, {name}! Want to play again?": [393.838, 3.103], "Well done, explorer! Here is a Tidewalk sticker. The bridge is open: Port Lumen is just ahead!": [397.391, 5.897], "THE TIDEWALK. Low tide! Port Lumen \u2192 across the sand and the rope bridges.": [403.738, 4.916], "THE OLD DOCK. At high tide there is only sea here. At low tide\u2026 who knows?": [409.104, 4.596], "THE TIDEWALK. Lighthouse Island \u2190 across the sand and the rope bridges. Walk only at low tide!": [414.15, 6.687], "{name}, you beat all five Tidewalk explorers!": [421.287, 2.356], "That\u2019s the gold Tidewalk sticker! Look for it in your notebook, next to your treasures.": [424.093, 4.596], "The X isn't here anyway. Look: it's on an island far to the southeast. We'll find it first! Come on, crew!": [429.139, 6.431], "The old sea map is back in its case. The X is far to the southeast\u2026": [436.019, 4.447], "Look at that X\u2026 on an island far to the southeast. I wonder what's there.": [440.916, 4.319], "Gus (in the Clock Tower)": [445.685, 1.545], "Gus in the Clock Tower": [447.68, 1.481], "Mayor Bea (in the Town Hall)": [449.611, 1.652], "Mayor Bea in the Town Hall": [451.713, 1.524], "Pedro (by the Town Hall Plaza)": [453.687, 2.015], "Pedro by the Town Hall Plaza": [456.152, 1.993], "Captain Lin (in the Harbor Office)": [458.595, 1.993], "Captain Lin in the Harbor Office": [461.039, 1.865], "Rafi (at the fish market by the harbor)": [463.354, 2.377], "Rafi at the fish market by the harbor": [466.181, 2.228], "Coco (in the Ice Cream Parlor)": [468.859, 1.951], "Coco in the Ice Cream Parlor": [471.26, 1.908], "Pepper (in the Galleria)": [473.618, 1.417], "Pepper in the Galleria": [475.485, 1.417], "Mr. Fitz (in the Galleria)": [477.353, 1.759], "Mr. Fitz in the Galleria": [479.561, 1.673], "Dr. Kai (in the City Aquarium)": [481.685, 2.057], "Dr. Kai in the City Aquarium": [484.192, 1.972], "Ms. Reyes (in the City Library)": [486.614, 1.929], "Ms. Reyes in the City Library": [488.993, 1.887], "Dr. Amara (in the Museum)": [491.33, 1.908], "Dr. Amara in the Museum": [493.688, 1.823], "Olive (in the greenhouse, City Park)": [495.961, 2.121], "Olive in the greenhouse, City Park": [498.532, 2.036], "Mr. Bloom (on Market Street)":